# SCRUM-89 — response headers for the two association files.
#
# Format (same as Pages): a path line, then indented "Name: value" lines.
# Parsed by Workers; this file is never served as a static asset.
#
# Why it exists: Apple requires the file be named `apple-app-site-association`
# **without an extension**, so — unlike `assetlinks.json` — its content type
# cannot be inferred from the filename. Pinning it removes the doubt.
#
# Apple's currently documented hosting requirements for this file are:
#   "You must host the file using https:// with a valid certificate and with no
#    redirects."                                                (developer.apple.com)
# ⚠️ That "no redirects" is why public/_redirects must never touch /.well-known/.
/.well-known/apple-app-site-association
  Content-Type: application/json

# `.json` would be inferred correctly from the extension; pinned anyway, so the
# header does not depend on the host's behaviour.
/.well-known/assetlinks.json
  Content-Type: application/json
